From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:52:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: pcie: lock the parent bridge's config space for the
 reset on resume

With pm_reset the device is reset on resume by pci_reset_function_locked(),
since the PM core already holds the device lock. The chip has no FLR, so
this is a secondary bus reset of the parent bridge, and unlike
pci_reset_function() this path does not lock the bridge. The PCI core
warns once per boot, on the first resume:

  pcieport 0000:00:1d.0: unlocked secondary bus reset via: __pci_reset_function_locked+0x60/0x110

Lock the bridge's config space around the reset, as pci_dev_lock() does
for pci_reset_function(), so that no config access to the bridge races
the reset. The bridge's device lock is not taken: the PM core holds the
device's own lock, and taking the parent's after it would invert the lock
order.
---
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c    | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 9342fc6..6d0175c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2751,12 +2751,22 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(pm_reset, "Remove the device for system sleep, reset and probe
 
 static int brcmf_pcie_pm_reprobe(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
+	struct pci_dev *bridge = pci_upstream_bridge(pdev);
 	int err;
 
 	/* The PM core holds the device lock across the resume callbacks.
 	 * The reset_done handler probes the device after a reset.
+	 *
+	 * The reset is a secondary bus reset of the parent bridge. Its config
+	 * space is locked for it, as pci_reset_function() does through
+	 * pci_dev_lock(); only the config space, since taking the bridge's
+	 * device lock after the device's own would invert the lock order.
 	 */
+	if (bridge)
+		pci_cfg_access_lock(bridge);
 	err = pci_reset_function_locked(pdev);
+	if (bridge)
+		pci_cfg_access_unlock(bridge);
 	if (dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev))
 		return 0;
 	if (err)
